<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    Valid per-architecture C type spelling (`option ctypes on|off`).

    kuna's core types are literally NAMED uint1/int4/float8/float10/code, a
    verbatim port of upstream's no-<coretypes> fallback branch, which the real
    Ghidra application never takes because its Java side ships its own names over
    the wire. The printer prints those names, so none of them is valid C. The
    existing `realtypes` relabel (DIV-6) covers only residual TYPE_UNKNOWN, which
    is why one function can render `unsigned int` beside `int4`.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture. Both passes clear it
    and load the same real x86-64 ELF fixture, so the spelling is resolved
    against that target's decoded <data_organization> rather than the harness's.

    Pass 1 (`option ctypes off`, the shipped catalog default, which is what this
    corpus runs at: since 42 datatest assertions pin the Ghidra spellings)
    reproduces the vocabulary: `int4 printf(...)` and a `(uint8)` cast.

    Pass 2 (`option ctypes on`, which the `aggressive` preset selects, and
    `auto` selects that for anything under 500 KiB) spells the same types as the
    target's own C compiler would: `int` and `unsigned long`. `unsigned long` and
    not `unsigned long long` is the load-bearing part: x86-64 System V is LP64,
    where `long` is 8 bytes. The ILP32 counterpart (the same core type spelling
    `long long` because `long` is 4 there) is pinned by the companion Rust gate
    `ctypes_per_arch`, which needs two architectures in one process.

    Assertions span the combined output of both passes.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/fmt_x86_64</com>
  <com>option ctypes off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function printf</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function main</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/fmt_x86_64</com>
  <com>option ctypes on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function printf</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function main</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
